NPCs: {
	ScarabSultan: {
		DisplayName: Scarab Sultan
		Bestiary: A golden scarab king that flies the dunes with its sun held in its legs. It draws the path of every ball it kicks before it kicks it, which is the only courtesy it shows.
	}

	SandRoller: {
		DisplayName: Sand Roller
		Bestiary: A dung beetle the size of a dog. Its ball is a shield until it sends it rolling at you - and then it is just a beetle.
	}

	DustDevil: {
		DisplayName: Dust Devil
		Bestiary: A whirlwind with a dead scarab turning in its eye. When the ring of grit closes, it breathes in, and everything near it is pulled toward the middle.
	}

	RimeColossus: {
		DisplayName: The Rime
		Bestiary: An old spirit of the mountain, packed snow over a heart of glacier. It carries a block of ice the size of a boulder and has been walking the same snowfields since before anyone named them.
	}

	DriftHare: {
		DisplayName: Drift Hare
		Bestiary: It runs under the snow, and the only thing you see is the heap moving toward you - and two black ear tips. When the heap stops under your feet, step away.
	}

	FrostWisp: {
		DisplayName: Frost Wisp
		Bestiary: A flicker of cold that crosses and recrosses the air in front of you. It barely hurts to touch; what it leaves hanging behind it does.
	}

	OldShellback: {
		DisplayName: Old Shellback
		Bestiary: An ancient hermit crab that outgrew every shell the sea could offer, and took a sunken ship's hull instead. It still carries the cannon.
	}

	BarnacleCrab: {
		DisplayName: Barnacle Crab
		Bestiary: So crusted with barnacles it barely feels a blow. Hit it once and it clamps shut; leave it be, and it comes out lunging.
	}

	ScavengerGull: {
		DisplayName: Scavenger Gull
		Bestiary: It wheels over the beach doing no harm at all - until it stops, cries, and dives along the line it has picked.
	}

	ThornbackBoar: {
		DisplayName: Thornback Boar
		Bestiary: A forest boar that rolled in brambles until they took root. It scrapes the ground before it charges, and once it has picked its line, it does not turn.
	}

	LanternMole: {
		DisplayName: Lantern Mole
		Bestiary: Nobody knows who strapped the first lantern to a mole. The light moving behind the cave wall is the only warning before the ground breaks open.
	}

	PitcherSnapper: {
		DisplayName: Pitcher Snapper
		Bestiary: A jungle pitcher that grew tired of waiting for insects to fall in. It swells, then lobs its digestive acid at wherever its meal was standing.
	}

	HollowHarvester: {
		DisplayName: Hollow Harvester
		Bestiary: A scarecrow that outlived its field. It still keeps the crows off - by sending them at whatever comes near - and it still knows how far its scythe can reach.
	}

	Ronin: {
		DisplayName: Ronin
		Bestiary: A swordsman who outlived his lord and traded the katana for the kama. He says the field is honest work. He does not say what grows in it.

		TownNPCMood: {
			Content: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.Content}"
			NoHome: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.NoHome}"
			FarFromHome: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.FarFromHome}"
			LoveSpace: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.LoveSpace}"
			DislikeCrowded: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.DislikeCrowded}"
			HateCrowded: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.HateCrowded}"
			LikeBiome: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.LikeBiome}"
			DislikeBiome: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.DislikeBiome}"
			LikeNPC: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.LikeNPC}"
			DislikeNPC: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Ronin.DislikeNPC}"
			LikeNPC_Princess: I like {NPCName}.
			Princess_LovesNPC: I like {NPCName}.
		}
	}

	DormantEye: {
		DisplayName: The Dormant Eye
		Bestiary: A boulder with a lid grown shut over it. Knock the slabs off or wait for the lid to split, because the rock itself barely feels you.
	}

	EyePlate: {
		DisplayName: Eye Plate
		Bestiary: A slab of the crust the Dormant Eye grew instead of a shell.
	}

	KeeperOfTheRift: {
		DisplayName: Keeper of the Rift
		Bestiary: A shattered core that refuses to fall apart. Break its plates or punish the moment it opens its eye, because nothing else gets through.
	}

	KeeperPlate: {
		DisplayName: Keeper Plate
		Bestiary: A slab of the Keeper's shell, orbiting the thing it protects until it is thrown.
	}

	Riftling: {
		DisplayName: Riftling
		Bestiary: A splinter of something far larger, still carrying enough of the rift to hold itself together.
	}

	Mirrorling: {
		DisplayName: Mirrorling
		Bestiary: It does not follow you. It repeats you, half a second late and the wrong way round, so running is what brings it closer.
	}

	HollowEcho: {
		DisplayName: Hollow Echo
		Bestiary: Stone means nothing to it, so it announces itself instead. The sound it makes before a charge is the only warning you get, and it is enough.
	}

	Weaverling: {
		DisplayName: Weaverling
		Bestiary: Alone it is barely a threat. In pairs it strings a thread between itself and its neighbour, and the thread is the part that kills you.
	}

	RiftColossus: {
		DisplayName: Rift Colossus
		Bestiary: It does not go around the wall. Whatever arena you end up fighting it in is one that it dug.
	}

	WeaverOfTheRift: {
		DisplayName: Weaver of the Rift
		Bestiary: A loom that walks. It drives its own legs into the ground as anchors and strings the arena between them, and behind enough fabric it cannot be touched at all.
	}

	WeaverAnchor.DisplayName: Anchor Leg

	ShardSwarm: {
		DisplayName: Shard Swarm
		Bestiary: Eight pieces that have agreed to be one thing. Cut enough of them away and the agreement lapses.
	}

	NullWarden: {
		DisplayName: Null Warden
		Bestiary: Nothing touches it while the eye is shut. It stops chasing to open it, which is the only bargain it offers.
	}

	FirstKeeper: {
		DisplayName: The First Keeper
		Bestiary: It has been open since before the crack. It does not aim at you - it looks, and while it is looking at you the two of you can hurt each other twice as easily. Its lids are what narrow the eye; cutting one is a bargain, not a chore.
	}

	KeeperLid: {
		DisplayName: Keeper Lid
		Bestiary: A slab grown over the First Keeper's eye. It is not armour - it is how little of the world the eye can see.
	}

	KeeperEcho: {
		DisplayName: Keeper Echo
		Bestiary: A splinter of the First Keeper that got loose, still doing the only thing it knows. Meet three of them and you have been taught the whole fight.
	}

	FissureSlime: {
		DisplayName: Fissure Slime
		Bestiary: It swallowed the rock it was sitting on and never digested it. Killing it does not finish it - it comes apart into three that are still moving.
	}

	FissureSlimelet: {
		DisplayName: Fissure Slimelet
		Bestiary: A piece of a larger one, carrying on as though nothing happened.
	}

	Hangstone: {
		DisplayName: Hangstone
		Bestiary: It waits on the ceiling for something to walk under it. The rattle before it lets go is the only warning it gives, and it is enough.
	}

	FacetBeetle: {
		DisplayName: Facet Beetle
		Bestiary: It eats fissurite and carries what it has not digested. Easier to kill than a vein is to find.
	}

	Voidfly: {
		DisplayName: Voidfly
		Bestiary: The only thing in the crack that wants nothing from you. It will not fight and it will not stay still.
	}

	Spall: {
		DisplayName: Spall
		Bestiary: A slab that grew a front and hides behind it. Hitting the face it shows you is nearly pointless. Get behind it.
	}

	PlateBearer: {
		DisplayName: Plate Bearer
		Bestiary: It found one of the Keeper's plates and worked out which way to hold it. The plate is a budget, not a second health bar - spend it and there is an ordinary enemy underneath.
	}

	RiftReaper: {
		DisplayName: Rift Reaper
		Bestiary: It hangs back, draws a line across the cavern, and then is standing where the line ended.
	}

	FacetBroodmother: {
		DisplayName: Facet Broodmother
		Bestiary: A beetle that got old and kept laying. Rare, and worth a tier of ore in one sitting.
	}

	PlateShepherd: {
		DisplayName: Plate Shepherd
		Bestiary: It does not wear a plate. It carries spares, and hands one to whichever of its escort has just lost theirs.
	}

	BreachMouth: {
		DisplayName: Breach Mouth
		Bestiary: A crack that has decided to be a door. It cannot reach you, and it never stops handing you things that can.
	}

	Heave: {
		DisplayName: The Heave
		Bestiary: One plate of rock shoved up over another, and still moving. It does not chase you across the arena. It rearranges the arena.
	}

	Sifter: {
		DisplayName: The Sifter
		Bestiary: It came up with the rest of the ejecta and then declined to go back. It will take that rock off your hands.

		TownNPCMood: {
			Princess_LovesNPC: I like {NPCName}.
			LikeNPC_Princess: I like {NPCName}.
			HateCrowded: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Sifter.HateCrowded}"
			DislikeCrowded: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Sifter.DislikeCrowded}"
			LoveSpace: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Sifter.LoveSpace}"
			FarFromHome: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Sifter.FarFromHome}"
			NoHome: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Sifter.NoHome}"
			Content: "{$Mods.Terrapex.TownNPCMood.Sifter.Content}"
		}
	}
}

